3. README: how to customize
Photo: Save a square, clear photo as assets/profile.jpg. Until then, the initials “ASA” show instead.
Social links: Find const profileLinks near the top of the <script>. Paste each full URL (starting with https://) between the quotes. Any empty entry stays hidden.
WhatsApp: Hidden by default so your number isn’t public. To show it, change showWhatsApp: false to true.
CV: Put your PDF at assets/Abu_Saleh_Ahmed_CV.pdf. Once the site is published, the button hides itself and shows a friendly message if the file is missing.
Text changes: Experience, education, training and skills are in the jobs, edu, training and skills lists in the script. Edit the text inside the quotes only.
Colors: They are defined at the top of the CSS (--navy and --blue).
4. Free publishing with GitHub Pages
Create a free account at github.com.
Tap New repository, name it abusaleh-portfolio, set it to Public, and create it.
Tap Add file → Upload files. Upload index.html, then upload the assets folder (or its files), and tap Commit changes.
Open Settings → Pages. Under Branch, choose main and / (root), then Save.
After 1–2 minutes your site is live at https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/abusaleh-portfolio/. No paid domain is needed.

Local testing: Save the code as index.html on your computer or Android phone and open it in Chrome. On Android, a file manager can open it with Chrome.

